From e991c24d9c1e625474087f250fe8c0f6a6d096f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MOhammed Ali Shihab K <mohamk@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 11:10:52 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Subject: i2c: imx-lpi2c: revert clock prepare/unprepare from
 runtime PM path

ERR_FATAL_OUT crash notification is driven through a PCAL6408 I2C GPIO
expander. During kernel panic, the sideband panic notifier attempts to
assert ERR_FATAL_OUT by performing an I2C transaction.

After commit MLK-16713 ("i2c: imx-lpi2c: add clock prepare/unprepare to
clock resource management in runtime PM"), the LPI2C runtime resume path
was changed from:

    clk_bulk_enable()

to:

    clk_bulk_prepare_enable()

On i.MX95, clock preparation triggers SCMI clock operations. During
panic handling, the I2C transfer enters the runtime PM resume path and
blocks in:

    lpi2c_runtime_resume()
      -> clk_bulk_prepare_enable()
      -> clk_prepare()
      -> scmi_clk_enable()
      -> scmi_wait_for_reply()

This results in scheduling activity and RCU warnings while panic
processing is already in progress, preventing reliable completion of the
I2C transaction. Consequently, ERR_FATAL_OUT remains asserted and the
SA525M modem fails to detect the crash indication.

Restore the previous behaviour by using clk_bulk_enable() /
clk_bulk_disable() instead of clk_bulk_prepare_enable() /
clk_bulk_disable_unprepare() in the runtime PM path. This avoids the
SCMI clock prepare sequence during panic-time GPIO expander updates and
restores correct ERR_FATAL_OUT signalling.

Observed on:
  - i.MX95 + SA525M fusion platform
  - ERR_FATAL_OUT connected through PCAL6408 I2C GPIO expander
  - Kernel 6.18.x regression relative to 6.12.x

Signed-off-by: Mohammed Ali Shihab K <mohamk@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-imx-lpi2c.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-imx-lpi2c.c b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-imx-lpi2c.c
index 3e6ada070799..5c31cec8290f 100644
--- a/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-imx-lpi2c.c
+++ b/drivers/i2c/busses/i2c-imx-lpi2c.c
@@ -1589,7 +1589,7 @@ static int __maybe_unused lpi2c_runtime_suspend(struct device *dev)
 	if (lpi2c_imx->hwdata->is_irqsteer_interrupt)
 		devm_free_irq(lpi2c_imx->adapter.dev.parent, lpi2c_imx->irq, lpi2c_imx);
 
-	clk_bulk_disable_unprepare(lpi2c_imx->num_clks, lpi2c_imx->clks);
+	clk_bulk_disable(lpi2c_imx->num_clks, lpi2c_imx->clks);
 	pinctrl_pm_select_sleep_state(dev);
 
 	return 0;
@@ -1601,7 +1601,7 @@ static int __maybe_unused lpi2c_runtime_resume(struct device *dev)
 	int ret;
 
 	pinctrl_pm_select_default_state(dev);
-	ret = clk_bulk_prepare_enable(lpi2c_imx->num_clks, lpi2c_imx->clks);
+	ret = clk_bulk_enable(lpi2c_imx->num_clks, lpi2c_imx->clks);
 	if (ret) {
 		dev_err(dev, "failed to enable I2C clock, ret=%d\n", ret);
 		return ret;
-- 
